@startuml IAMS_VisitScheduling_Sequence_Supervisor
' Supervisor publishes calendar dates — matches IAMS implementation
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 8

title Visit Scheduling — Supervisor publishes dates (IAMS)

actor "Institutional\nSupervisor" as Sup

box "Presentation" #E8EAF6
  participant "User Interface\n(React)" as UI
end box

box "Application (PHP REST API)" #E3F2FD
  participant "VisitScheduleAPI\n(supervisor_visit_schedule.php)" as API
  participant "VisitScheduleHelper\n(visit_schedule_helpers.php)" as VS
  participant "NotificationService\n(notification_helpers.php)" as NS
end box

== Load schedule ==

Sup -> UI: Login & Navigate to\nVisit Scheduling

UI -> API: **loadVisitSchedule()**\nGET /api/supervisor/visit-schedule

API -> API: validateSupervisorSession()

API -> VS: **getAvailability**(lecturerId)
VS -> VS: query supervisor_visit_availability
VS --> API: List<VisitDate>

API -> VS: **getSelectionsByDate**(lecturerId)
VS -> VS: query student_visit_selections\nJOIN industrial_registration
VS --> API: Map<date, students[]>

API -> VS: **getAssignedStudentCount**(lecturerId)
VS --> API: count

API --> UI: JSON:\navailability,\nselections_by_date,\nassigned_students_count

UI --> Sup: Display calendar\n(student count per date)

== Publish dates ==

Sup -> UI: **toggleDates** on calendar\nclick **Save & notify students**

UI -> API: **saveAvailability**(dates,\nsync=true, notify_students=true)\nPOST /api/supervisor/visit-schedule

alt [At least one date selected]

  API -> VS: **normalizeDates**(dates)
  VS --> API: valid date keys

  API -> VS: **syncAvailability**(lecturerId, dates)
  VS -> VS: DELETE stale rows &\nrelated student_visit_selections
  VS -> VS: INSERT IGNORE new dates
  VS --> API: synced

  API -> VS: **publishAvailability**(lecturerId)
  VS -> VS: SET published_at = NOW()\nWHERE lecturer_id = …
  VS --> API: published

  API -> NS: **notifyStudentsVisitSchedulePublished**\n(lecturerId, supervisorName, dates)

  NS -> NS: **createInSystemAlert**()\nfor each assigned student

  note right of NS
    In-system notifications only
    (student_notifications table).
    No automated email.
  end note

  NS --> API: notifications created

  API --> UI: { success: true,\nnotified: true }

  UI --> Sup: **Visit dates published**\nsuccessfully

else [No dates selected]

  API --> UI: validation error

  UI --> Sup: **Error:** select at least\none date on the calendar

end

@enduml

@startuml IAMS_VisitScheduling_Sequence_Student
' Student selects preferred visit day(s) from published calendar
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12

title Visit Scheduling — Student selects dates (IAMS)

actor "Student" as Stu

box "Presentation" #E8EAF6
  participant "User Interface\n(React)" as UI
end box

box "Application (PHP REST API)" #E3F2FD
  participant "VisitScheduleAPI\n(student_visit_schedule.php)" as API
  participant "VisitScheduleHelper\n(visit_schedule_helpers.php)" as VS
  participant "NotificationService\n(notification_helpers.php)" as NS
end box

== Load published dates ==

Stu -> UI: Login & Navigate to\nVisit Schedule

UI -> API: **loadVisitSchedule()**\nGET /api/student/visit-schedule

API -> VS: **getLecturerForStudent**(indexNumber)

alt [Supervisor assigned]

  VS --> API: lecturerId, supervisor profile

  API -> VS: **getPublishedAvailability**(lecturerId)
  note right of VS
    Only rows where
    published_at IS NOT NULL
  end note
  VS --> API: List<VisitDate>

  API -> VS: **getMySelections**(indexNumber, lecturerId)
  VS --> API: List<Selection>

  API --> UI: JSON:\nsupervisor, availability,\nmy_selections

  UI --> Stu: Display published dates\n(highlight own selections)

else [No supervisor assigned]

  VS --> API: null

  API --> UI: { supervisor: null,\navailability: [] }

  UI --> Stu: **Message:** No institutional\nsupervisor assigned yet

end

== Submit selections ==

Stu -> UI: **selectDates** on calendar\nclick **Submit selections**

UI -> API: **submitSelections**(dates)\nPOST /api/student/visit-schedule

alt [All dates valid & published]

  API -> VS: **validateDates**(dates, lecturerId)
  VS -> VS: check against\npublished availability map
  VS --> API: valid

  API -> VS: **replaceSelections**(indexNumber,\nlecturerId, dates)
  VS -> VS: DELETE old rows;\nINSERT student_visit_selections
  VS --> API: saved

  API -> NS: **notifySupervisorVisitSelection**\n(lecturerId, student, dates)

  NS -> NS: **createInSystemAlert**()\nfor institutional supervisor

  NS --> API: notification created

  API --> UI: { success: true, dates }

  UI --> Stu: **Selections saved.**\nSupervisor notified.

else [Date not available]

  API -> VS: **validateDates**(dates, lecturerId)
  VS --> API: invalid date key

  API --> UI: HTTP 400:\ndate not available for booking

  UI --> Stu: **Error:** invalid date\nselected — choose a\npublished date

end

@enduml

@startuml IAMS_VisitScheduling_Sequence_Combined
' Single-page overview: supervisor publish then student select
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

title Visit Scheduling — End-to-end sequence (IAMS)

actor "Institutional\nSupervisor" as Sup
actor "Student" as Stu

participant "User Interface\n(React)" as UI
participant "VisitScheduleAPI\n(PHP REST)" as API
participant "VisitScheduleHelper" as VS
participant "NotificationService" as NS

== A. Supervisor publishes visit dates ==

Sup -> UI: Open Visit Scheduling
UI -> API: GET supervisor/visit-schedule
API -> VS: load availability & selections
VS --> API: data
API --> UI: calendar data
UI --> Sup: Show calendar

Sup -> UI: Toggle dates → Save & notify
UI -> API: POST { dates, sync, notify_students: true }
API -> VS: sync + publish (published_at)
API -> NS: notifyStudentsVisitSchedulePublished()
NS -> NS: createInSystemAlert (students)
NS --> API: ok
API --> UI: success
UI --> Sup: Dates published

== B. Student selects preferred day(s) ==

Stu -> UI: Open Visit Schedule
UI -> API: GET student/visit-schedule
API -> VS: get published dates only
VS --> API: availability + my_selections
API --> UI: calendar data
UI --> Stu: Show published dates

Stu -> UI: Select dates → Submit
UI -> API: POST { dates }
API -> VS: validate + save selections
API -> NS: notifySupervisorVisitSelection()
NS -> NS: createInSystemAlert (supervisor)
NS --> API: ok
API --> UI: success
UI --> Stu: Selections saved

Sup -> UI: Refresh Visit Scheduling
UI -> API: GET supervisor/visit-schedule
API --> UI: selections_by_date updated
UI --> Sup: View students by date

@enduml
